  <h2>Why we began</h2>
  <p>
    Saa Thum began with a simple wish: that any family, anywhere, could have a puja done properly —
    without travel, without hunting for a priest, and without anyone frightening them into it. We
    perform pujas and havans that celebrate life: exams passed, homes blessed, health restored,
    families united, festivals kept.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Choose your ritual.</strong> Pick a puja or a havan — by what you're hoping for, by deity, or by festival.</li>
    <li><strong>Tell us your sankalp.</strong> Your name, gotra and wish. Our priest speaks them at the altar.</li>
    <li><strong>Watch it live.</strong> Light a lamp at home, join the aarti at the close, and watch the replay for 7 days.</li>
    <li><strong>Receive prasad.</strong> If you'd like, we post prasad to your door after the ritual.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Pujas and havans, nothing else</h2>
  <p>
    That's all we do, and we do it well. Our priests are ours; the experience is ours; the
    responsibility is ours. See every ritual on <a href="/marketplace">Our Pujas</a>, or read
    <a href="/how-it-works">how it works</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every ritual we perform is benefic — for learning, prosperity, health, love, peace and
    celebration. We don't do fear, we don't do fierce rituals, and we never tell you something bad
    will happen if you don't book.
  </p>
  <div class="note">
    Rituals are performed with devotion by verified priests. Benefits described are those
    traditionally sought by devotees; Saa Thum makes no claims of guaranteed outcomes.
  </div>

  <h2>What we value</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your name, spoken properly.</strong> The sankalp carries your name, gotra and wish, and you hear it at the altar.</li>
    <li><strong>The full price, upfront.</strong> What you see before you book is what you pay. Refunds follow our <a href="/refunds">refund policy</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Only joy.</strong> No fear-based selling, no guarantees, no scary predictions.</li>
    <li><strong>Say what is true.</strong> We are early, and we say so clearly rather than burying it.</li>
  </ul>

